From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5sd <ps5sd@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] server: the gallery as one ZIP, streamed

GET /ps5sd/v1/gallery/archive sends every kept file of --output-dir as a ZIP,
and a POST with names=<file names> (a form a page submits) or a GET with
?names= sends the ones named. The names are checked as the route of a single
file checks them, and an image that is not kept (tmp_) is left out. A file
with parameters in .thumbs/<name>.txt (a video's, a PNG saved without
metadata) brings them as <name>.txt.

The archive is made while it is sent (zip_stream.cpp, chunked): one piece of
a file is in memory, whatever the gallery's size. The entries are stored, with
data descriptors, so the CRC-32 is made while the file is read; ZIP64 records
come with a file of 4 GiB or more, 65535 files or more, or an offset past
4 GiB. A file that vanished after the listing is left out.

The form's POST with only the login cookie needs no X-PS5SD-Request header (a
form cannot add it): the route only reads, and the cookie is SameSite=Strict.
